    <briefdescription>
<para>Keeps track of all <ref refid="structcsmp_1_1_index" kindref="compound">Index</ref> objects once they have been registered. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Serves <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_property_database" kindref="compound">PropertyDatabase</ref> to keep all existing <ref refid="structcsmp_1_1_index" kindref="compound">Index</ref> objects objects up to date, which is necessary when new variables are created at runtime.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>index tracking is necessary because some classes have indices as members. These objects can get invalidated when new variables of the same kind and place. are created. If so, for instance, the 5th scalar on the node might become the 10th.</para>
</simplesect>
By tracking all <ref refid="structcsmp_1_1_index" kindref="compound">Index</ref> objects that exist in a model, these can be updated by the <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_property_database" kindref="compound">PropertyDatabase</ref> everytime a variable is created or deleted.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>this implementation is based on the &quot;Observer&quot; design pattern.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="author"><para>P. Lang </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>9/25/2012</para>
</simplesect>
